---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy · ModeDock"
  description="What ModeDock's optional, anonymous usage data holds, what it never collects, and how to turn it off."
>
  <article class="doc wrap">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      ModeDock works without sending anything. If you agree, it sends anonymous counts of the features you use. They
      tell me what to improve.
    </p>

    <h2>Off until you say yes</h2>
    <p>
      On first launch ModeDock asks: <em>Share anonymous usage data?</em> Nothing is sent unless you choose Share. You
      can change this any time in Settings → General.
    </p>

    <h2>What is sent</h2>
    <p>About every 8 hours, and only if something was counted:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>How often you used each feature, like opening the panel or changing brightness. Only the count, never what was on screen.</li>
      <li>How ModeDock is set up, like how many profiles and external screens you have. Never their names.</li>
      <li>The app and macOS version, the app's language, and whether the Mac is Apple silicon or Intel.</li>
      <li>
        A random install ID. It's made when you opt in and deleted when you opt out, and it isn't tied to you, your Mac or
        your Apple account.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>To see a report exactly as it's sent, use Show Data… in Settings → General.</p>

    <h2>What the server adds</h2>
    <p>
      The day the report arrived and your country. Cloudflare, which runs the server, looks up the country. The server
      doesn't read or store your IP address, and its logs are off.
    </p>

    <h2>What is never collected</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your name, email, Apple account or anything you type</li>
      <li>IP addresses, serial numbers or other hardware IDs</li>
      <li>Names of screens, profiles or files, and file contents</li>
      <li>Screenshots or anything on your screens</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Where it's kept</h2>
    <p>
      In a Cloudflare database in the European Union, through <code>telemetry.modedock.app</code>. Only the ModeDock
      maintainer can read it.
    </p>

    <h2>What is made public</h2>
    <p>
      The home page shows totals for the last 30 days: active installs, the most used features, macOS versions and
      countries. Each number covers at least 5 installs, so nobody can be picked out. Install IDs and single reports are
      never published.
    </p>

    <h2>Turning it off</h2>
    <p>
      Uncheck Share anonymous usage statistics in Settings → General. ModeDock stops sending and deletes its install ID and
      its counts. If you turn it back on, you get a new install ID.
    </p>
    <p>
      To delete reports already sent, open an issue on{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/ilijamt/modedock/issues">GitHub</a> with the install ID shown in Show Data…, before you
      turn sharing off.
    </p>

    <h2>The code</h2>
    <p>
      The app and the server are both open source: see{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/ilijamt/modedock/blob/main/Packages/ModeDockKit/Sources/ModeDockCore/Telemetry.swift">Telemetry.swift</a>{" "}
      and <a href="https://github.com/ilijamt/modedock/tree/main/server/telemetry">server/telemetry</a>.
    </p>

    <p class="updated">Last updated 15 November 2026.</p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
